{
  "_doc": "Stream E (M2). The event director's list (PLAN §5.2). `director` = the realm rules (ONE big event at a time, sized to who is online and in band, announced 10 minutes ahead, waystone travel to it free while it runs). `realm` = the big events, each on a schedule or a trigger; the province world boss Grimtallow is a fixed-time scheduled event. `zone` = the per-zone event bosses, each running on its own in every zone copy at stream B's event arena (`site` = the arena id in data/zones/<world zone>/placements.json): two waves from the zone's camp mix, then the boss (an encounter script id in data/encounters/). Everyone within autoEnrolMetres joins a temporary event group (PLAN §5.3). Times are real minutes; reward xp = share of a level's XP, gold = multiple of a kill's gold (data/quests/README.md). Every event carries a `blurb` (one or two sentences for the map and the event card: what happens and what to do). Play-test 3 R3: nothing waits on a real-time clock except the world boss's fixed schedule; events start when someone comes near (director.startOn 'near', director.zone), after a short countdown shown as a real number, and are sized for fewer than 5 players.",
  "director": {
    "oneRealmEventAtATime": true,
    "announceMinutes": 10,
    "reminderMinutes": [
      5,
      1
    ],
    "freeWaystoneTravel": true,
    "gapMinutes": [
      10,
      20
    ],
    "inBandLevels": 3,
    "size": {
      "healthPerPlayer": 0.35,
      "addWavePerPlayers": 2,
      "minPlayers": 1,
      "capPlayers": 5,
      "note": "Play-test 3 R3 — fewer than 5 players at a time: boss health x (1 + healthPerPlayer x (enrolled - 1)) up to capPlayers 5 (x2.4 for five), one extra add per addWavePerPlayers enrolled (two for five)."
    },
    "pick": "Play-test 3 R3 — the owner: 'events should activate when a player goes nearby, not wait in real time; fewer than 5 people will play at a time'. startOn 'near': a realm event starts when a player in its band comes within its radius + nearMetres (and its cooldown is over, and nothing else is running, and nearGapMinutes have passed since the last one), after a countdownSeconds countdown sent as a real time. A FIXED-schedule event (the world boss) is still announced announceMinutes ahead with its real start time (`at`), and also starts on demand when someone in band walks up and it has been quiet quietMinutes. Weighted events never start on their own.",
    "credit": "By contribution (damage, healing, soaks); loot is personal.",
    "startOn": "near",
    "nearMetres": 60,
    "countdownSeconds": 15,
    "nearGapMinutes": 3,
    "zone": {
      "startOn": "near",
      "nearMetres": 50,
      "countdownSeconds": 15,
      "cooldownMinutes": [
        3,
        5
      ],
      "_doc": "Play-test 3 R3 (stream A js/sim/province.js zoneEventsTick): a zone event waits at its arena, armed, until a player comes within the arena radius + nearMetres; then a countdown of countdownSeconds (sent as a real time, `zoneEvent {kind:'soon', at, inMs}`), then the waves. Everyone walking away during the countdown calls it off. After it ends it rests cooldownMinutes (the map shows when it is ready again: `kind:'cooldown', at`). No real-time schedule."
    }
  },
